if you're a product manager you need to  know exactly who your customers are what  they need and how they engage in your  product the key to obtaining this  information is user research  in this course i'll show you how to  apply user research to every stage of  the product life cycle to ensure the  success of your product in your team  let's use a research it's a process for  learning more about your customer by  going out and talking to them you can  learn really important things like what  your customers are actually doing and  thinking what feedback they have about  your product ideas and how they interact  with the design that you and your team  create it's like a secret weapon that  you use regularly to give you a sneak  peek into what's really going to happen  when you launch preventing hours of  heartache over unnecessary features and  poor design and it's so easy to do i  think everyone can learn it and  integrate it into their process to  create those once-in-a-lifetime products  that customers absolutely can't get  enough of i'll help you understand what  user research methods are out there when  to use them and how to use them  we'll deep dive into three key methods  rapid experimentation moderated and  unmoderated testing learning the skills  for each method so you can go out there  and do it yourself or support your team  in gathering data i am really passionate  about user research and i am thrilled to  share with you all the insider tips and  tricks for how to do a great job at all  aspects of testing from planning your  tests to recruiting subjects to  analyzing your data  see you in class
 

